INT. ORBITAL FERRY AIRLOCK - CONTINUOUS

A cramped airlock. Red warning strip lights pulse on the walls.

TECHNICIAN YUSUF BELLAMY, 30s, pressure suit, helmet off, bangs on the inner hatch with a gloved fist.

YUSUF
Control, I've got seal failure on lock two. Repeat, seal failure.

CONTROL (V.O.)
(over radio)
Copy lock two. Do not cycle the outer door.

YUSUF
I'm not cycling anything. Something's cycling it for me.

The outer door groans a hand's width open. Air shrieks out. Yusuf clips his tether to a rail and grabs the manual lever with both hands.

Behind him, the inner hatch pops. COMMANDER ISOLDE RAINES, 50s, bare-headed and furious, shoulders in and slaps a patch over the leak in one move. The shriek stops. The outer door shudders closed.

Silence. Both breathe.

ISOLDE
Stop shouting at the radio.

YUSUF
It was loud.

CONTROL (V.O.)
Lock two, status?

ISOLDE
(into her collar)
Sealed. Tell maintenance their gasket is a joke.

She hauls Yusuf upright by the harness. He laughs, shaky. She does not.
